# Rule: Git must never change the bytes of any file in this repository.
#
# Each attribute below turns off one way Git can rewrite bytes on checkout or
# add, whatever the machine's own config says:
#   -text                    no end-of-line conversion (core.autocrlf, core.eol),
#                            so a Windows clone with the Git for Windows default
#                            (autocrlf=true) still gets byte-exact files;
#   -ident                   no `$Id$` expansion;
#   -filter                  no smudge/clean filter (for example git-lfs, which
#                            is configured system-wide on some machines);
#   -working-tree-encoding   no re-encoding (for example to UTF-16).
# Scripture, red-letter offsets, checksums and golden data depend on that.
#
# This file overrides a user-level or system core.attributesFile. Only
# $GIT_DIR/info/attributes (local to one clone) and a .gitattributes in a
# subdirectory outrank it, so CI also checks that every content file's bytes
# equal its index blob (`git hash-object --no-filters`, see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml). Don't add .gitattributes files in subdirectories.
#
# Code line endings are not normalized by Git. rustfmt.toml enforces LF for
# Rust, and `cargo fmt --check` in CI fails on CRLF.
* -text -ident -filter -working-tree-encoding

# Binary formats: no text diff, no textual merge.
*.sqlite  binary
*.revpack binary
*.zip     binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.webp    binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary

# Content paths, listed explicitly. Keep these lines LAST: in .gitattributes
# the last matching line wins, so they stay byte-exact even if someone later
# adds a normalization rule (like `* text=auto` or `* ident`) above.
/sources/**                  -text -ident -filter -working-tree-encoding
/pipeline/tests/fixtures/**  -text -ident -filter -working-tree-encoding
**/golden/**                 -text -ident -filter -working-tree-encoding
**/*.sha256                  -text -ident -filter -working-tree-encoding
